OL,3,GNEWSAAre families tired of 'beige food'
OL,4,Aon kids' menus?
OL,5,
OL,6,FWould families in Guernsey like to see
OL,7,Fmore vegetables and fewer "beige"
OL,8,Foptions such as chicken nuggets on
OL,9,Fchildren's menus?
OL,11,FA healthy living charity is asking the
OL,12,Fquestion as the spotlight on more
OL,13,Fnutritional food in schools widens to
OL,14,Fthe hospitality sector and eating out.
OL,16,FCat Tyrrell, who is an eat well officer
OL,17,Fat the Health Improvement Commission
OL,18,Ffor Guernsey and Alderney, said the
OL,19,Forganisation was to survey parents,
OL,20,Fcarers and children on the subject
OL,21,Fbefore working "collaboratively" with
OL,22,Frestaurants on a healthier approach.
OL,23,APub: 05-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
